[b]Single player only. Build 42.[/b]
Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3661336777]Horse Mod[/url].

An add-on for the Horse mod. Aim and fire guns from the saddle, and tie your horse to a fence, pole or tree so it stays put while you loot.

[h2]How to use[/h2]
[list]
[*]Shooting: equip a gun while mounted, hold aim and click. The shot goes toward the mouse, in any direction by default. Hit chance drops 2 points at a walk, 5 at a trot and 20 at a gallop.
[*]From the saddle: ride up to a fence, pole, railing, lamp post, sign post or tree, right-click it and choose Dismount and tie to...
[*]On foot: right-click the post with a loose horse within 4 tiles and choose Tie (horse) to...
[*]Reins tie it for free. Without reins you need a Rope, which you get back when you untie.
[*]A tied horse stays within 2 tiles of the post. Untie with vanilla's Detach animal from..., or just mount it.
[/list]

[h2]Options[/h2]
Sandbox page "Horse Shooting & Hitching":
[list]
[*]Shooting from the saddle: on
[*]Hit chance penalty at a walk, trot and gallop: 2, 5 and 20
[*]Shooting arc, degrees each side of the horse's heading: 180 (all round; 90 is the front half)
[*]Tied horse range: 2 tiles
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Written against Horse mod 1.1.2.
[*]Single player only.
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*]Melee weapons, spears included, still can't attack from the saddle.
[*]Aiming uses the mouse, so on a controller you shoot along the horse's heading.
[*]Posts are recognized by tile name, so some fences or posts may not offer the tie option.
[/list]

Source and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/maxcwolf/pz-mods/tree/main/horse-shoot-and-hitch]GitHub[/url]
